@iseeyuan and I were debugging exporting llava. We ran into the following error message:
```
  File "/Users/myuan/miniconda3/envs/executorch/lib/python3.10/site-packages/torch/_dynamo/exc.py", line 172, in unimplemented
    raise Unsupported(msg)
torch._dynamo.exc.Unsupported: call_function BuiltinVariable(iter) [UserDefinedObjectVariable(Image)] {}
from user code:
   File "/Users/myuan/src/executorch/examples/models/llava/model.py", line 29, in forward
    images_tensor = process_images(
  File "/Users/myuan/src/LLaVA/llava/mm_utils.py", line 170, in process_images
    for image in images:
```
What this actually meant was: "You tried to call iter(images), but images is of type PIL.Image so Dynamo didn't know how to handle it, thus leading to a graph break". This was an error in the model code (`images` probably should have been a `List[Image]`instead of an `Image`), but the actual error "torch._dynamo.exc.Unsupported: call_function BuiltinVariable(iter) [UserDefinedObjectVariable(Image)] {}" is very obtuse.

